{%- comment -%}
  SHUDHI — Wishlist

  The saved-items band on /pages/wishlist. Styled in assets/shudhi-wishlist.css.

  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
  SEVEN THINGS HERE ARE LOAD-BEARING
  ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

  1. THE ROOT CARRIES `sh`. assets/shudhi-home.js:300 selects `.sh [data-reveal]`
     and adds .is-in; the CSS pre-state (shudhi-home.css:234) starts those
     elements at opacity 0. Without the bare class the furniture stays invisible
     for the life of the page. Same rule as sh-journal.liquid note 1.

  2. NOTHING HERE USES [data-reveal]. Two motion systems exist in this theme and
     nothing on this template loads assets/sh-story-motion.js, so [data-sh-reveal]
     was never an option — but the global [data-reveal] observer
     (assets/shudhi-home.js:298) is wrong here too: every element it would drive
     BOOTS HIDDEN, and its CSS pre-state is opacity 0. An element that is
     display:none when the observer starts depends on the observer re-firing once
     JS unhides it; if that does not happen the content is invisible for the life
     of the page. So the cards and both states carry their own CSS fade, keyed on
     .is-in, added by this file's JS after unhiding. --i is the card stagger.

  3. EVERY PRODUCT IS RENDERED, HIDDEN; JS REVEALS THE SAVED ONES. localStorage
     holds ONLY an array of product-id strings (assets/hov-wishlist.js:21) —
     no title, price or image is ever persisted, and /search/suggest.json
     returns nothing for a numeric id. Server-rendering the catalogue and
     filtering client-side buys real `money` formatting, real variant ids, no
     fetch, no skeleton and no empty-state flash.
     THE CEILING: `for product in collections.all.products` returns at most 50
     without {% paginate %}. This store publishes one product. Past ~50, either
     paginate here or fetch /products/<handle>.js per saved id.
     Safe to loop: the /collections/all redirect (layout/theme.liquid:98) is
     gated on `request.page_type == 'collection'` and cannot fire on a page.

  4. THE REMOVE CONTROL IS A REAL `.hov-wish__btn`. Rendering snippets/hov-wishlist
     inside the card hands the whole toggle to assets/hov-wishlist.js — the
     per-customer storage key, the legacy-key migration, the nav badge, the toast
     and the cross-tab BroadcastChannel. `toggleWishlist` is module-private, so
     re-implementing removal here would mean duplicating the storage contract.
     We only listen and re-hide. Its hot-pink active tint (#FF4D7A) is retinted
     to brand gold in the stylesheet — the JS writes fill/stroke as SVG
     PRESENTATION ATTRIBUTES, which any CSS rule outranks.

  5. THREE STATES, NOT TWO. assets/hov-wishlist.js:258 wraps every toggle in
     window.hovRequireLogin, so saving is login-gated: a signed-out shopper who
     taps a heart gets the login modal, never a save. Their list is therefore
     ALWAYS empty, and "your wishlist is empty" would be a lie — they get the
     sign-in state instead. Login state is read from the server-rendered
     <html data-customer-logged-in> (layout/theme.liquid:4), which is immune to
     JS timing and to bfcache restores.

  6. IT BOOTS IN data-state="loading". Neither the grid nor either empty state is
     painted until the JS has read localStorage, so nobody sees "your wishlist is
     empty" flash before their saved items appear.

  7. ADD TO CART IS A REAL FORM, NOT A FETCH. assets/ajax-cart.js.liquid:327
     delegates on `form[action^="/cart/add"]` and owns the POST, the drawer, the
     count and the cart:updated event; assets/hov-cart-checkout.js drives the
     button's busy state from the real click. Writing our own fetch here would
     bypass all four. Same contract as assets/sh-product.js:5-8.

  PORTABLE: this file + assets/shudhi-wishlist.css + the two snippets it renders.
{%- endcomment -%}

{{ 'shudhi-wishlist.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}

{%- assign s = section.settings -%}
{%- assign uid = section.id -%}

{%- comment -%}
  The catalogue fallback for the empty-state CTA: this store's single product,
  falling back to the all-products route if the catalogue is ever empty.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- assign first_product = collections.all.products.first -%}
{%- assign shop_url = s.empty_cta_link | default: first_product.url | default: routes.all_products_collection_url -%}

<section
  class="sh sh-wishlist{% if s.animate %} sh-wishlist--animate{% endif %}"
  data-sh-wishlist
  data-state="loading"
  style="--sh-wish-bg:{{ s.bg }};--sh-wish-pad-top:{{ s.pad_top }}px;--sh-wish-pad-bottom:{{ s.pad_bottom }}px;"
  aria-labelledby="sh-wish-count-{{ uid }}">
  <div class="sh-wrap">

    {%- comment -%} Saved count. aria-live so a removal is announced. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="sh-wish__bar" data-sh-wish-bar hidden>
      <p class="sh-wish__count" id="sh-wish-count-{{ uid }}" data-sh-wish-count aria-live="polite"></p>
    </div>

    <ul class="sh-wish__grid" role="list" data-sh-wish-grid hidden>
      {%- for product in collections.all.products -%}
        {%- assign variant = product.selected_or_first_available_variant -%}
        <li class="sh-wish__item" data-sh-wish-item data-product-id="{{ product.id }}" hidden>
          <article class="sh-wish__card">

            <div class="sh-wish__media">
              <a class="sh-wish__media-link" href="{{ product.url }}" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
                {%- if product.featured_image -%}
                  <img class="sh-wish__img"
                       src="{{ product.featured_image | image_url: width: 700 }}"
                       alt="{{ product.featured_image.alt | escape }}"
                       width="700" height="700" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                {%- else -%}
                  <span class="sh-wish__img sh-wish__img--empty">
                    {% render 'sh-icon', name: 'shudhi-mark' %}
                  </span>
                {%- endif -%}
              </a>

              {%- comment -%}
                Note 4: this is the remove control. hov-wishlist.js binds it,
                marks it .is-wishlisted on init and owns the un-save.
              {%- endcomment -%}
              {% render 'hov-wishlist', product: product %}
            </div>

            <div class="sh-wish__body">
              <h3 class="sh-wish__title">
                <a href="{{ product.url }}">{{ product.title }}</a>
              </h3>

              <p class="sh-wish__price">
                <span class="sh-wish__price-now">{{ product.price | money }}</span>
                {%- if product.compare_at_price > product.price -%}
                  <s class="sh-wish__price-was">{{ product.compare_at_price | money }}</s>
                {%- endif -%}
              </p>

              {%- if product.available -%}
                <form method="post" action="/cart/add" enctype="multipart/form-data" class="sh-wish__form">
                  <input type="hidden" name="id" value="{{ variant.id }}">
                  <input type="hidden" name="quantity" value="1">
                  <button type="submit" name="add" class="sh-btn sh-btn--solid sh-wish__atc">
                    {{ s.atc_label | default: 'Add to cart' }}
                  </button>
                </form>
              {%- else -%}
                <p class="sh-wish__soldout">{{ s.soldout_label | default: 'Sold out' }}</p>
              {%- endif -%}
            </div>

          </article>
        </li>
      {%- endfor -%}
    </ul>

    {%- comment -%} State 2: signed in, nothing saved. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="sh-wish__state" data-sh-wish-empty hidden>
      <span class="sh-wish__state-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'heart-line', sw: 1.1 %}</span>
      <h2 class="sh-wish__state-title sh-serif">{{ s.empty_title | default: 'Your wishlist is empty' }}</h2>
      {%- if s.empty_text != blank -%}
        <p class="sh-wish__state-text">{{ s.empty_text }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <a class="sh-btn sh-btn--solid sh-wish__state-cta" href="{{ shop_url }}">
        {{ s.empty_cta_label | default: 'Explore products' }}{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}
      </a>
    </div>

    {%- comment -%} State 1: signed out — note 5. {%- endcomment -%}
    <div class="sh-wish__state" data-sh-wish-guest hidden>
      <span class="sh-wish__state-icon" aria-hidden="true">{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'heart-line', sw: 1.1 %}</span>
      <h2 class="sh-wish__state-title sh-serif">{{ s.guest_title | default: 'Sign in to see your saved items' }}</h2>
      {%- if s.guest_text != blank -%}
        <p class="sh-wish__state-text">{{ s.guest_text }}</p>
      {%- endif -%}
      <a class="sh-btn sh-btn--solid sh-wish__state-cta" href="{{ routes.account_login_url }}">
        {{ s.guest_cta_label | default: 'Sign in' }}{% render 'sh-icon', name: 'arrow-right' %}
      </a>
      <p class="sh-wish__state-note">
        <a href="{{ routes.account_register_url }}">{{ s.guest_register_label | default: 'Create an account' }}</a>
      </p>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

<script>
/* SHUDHI — wishlist page. Reveals the server-rendered cards whose product id is
   in localStorage, and re-renders on every signal hov-wishlist.js emits.
   House conventions: IIFE, ES5-friendly, single-execution guard, boot on
   readyState, re-boot on shopify:section:load, per-root data-sh-init. */
(function () {
  'use strict';

  if (window.__shWishlist) return;
  window.__shWishlist = true;

  function loggedIn() {
    return document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-customer-logged-in') === 'true';
  }

  /* Must match assets/hov-wishlist.js:16 exactly, or the page reads a
     different list than the hearts write. */
  function storageKey() {
    var cid = document.documentElement.getAttribute('data-customer-id') || '';
    return cid ? 'hov_wishlist_' + cid : 'hov_wishlist';
  }

  function savedIds() {
    try {
      var raw = JSON.parse(localStorage.getItem(storageKey()));
      return Object.prototype.toString.call(raw) === '[object Array]' ? raw : [];
    } catch (e) {
      /* private mode, blocked storage, malformed JSON — an empty list is the
         honest answer and still renders a valid page. */
      return [];
    }
  }

  function init(root) {
    if (root.getAttribute('data-sh-init')) return;
    root.setAttribute('data-sh-init', '1');

    var bar   = root.querySelector('[data-sh-wish-bar]');
    var countEl = root.querySelector('[data-sh-wish-count]');
    var grid  = root.querySelector('[data-sh-wish-grid]');
    var empty = root.querySelector('[data-sh-wish-empty]');
    var guest = root.querySelector('[data-sh-wish-guest]');
    var items = [].slice.call(root.querySelectorAll('[data-sh-wish-item]'));

    /* The shared snippet's label reads "Add … to wishlist". On this page the
       button only ever removes, so relabel it once. */
    items.forEach(function (li) {
      var btn = li.querySelector('.hov-wish__btn');
      var title = li.querySelector('.sh-wish__title');
      if (btn && title) {
        btn.setAttribute('aria-label', 'Remove ' + title.textContent.trim() + ' from wishlist');
      }
    });

    /* Both states boot hidden, so they cannot rely on the global [data-reveal]
       observer — note 2. Unhide first, then add .is-in on the next frame so the
       transition has two distinct states to run between. */
    function showState(el) {
      el.hidden = false;
      if (window.requestAnimationFrame) {
        requestAnimationFrame(function () { el.classList.add('is-in'); });
      } else {
        el.classList.add('is-in');
      }
    }
    function hideState(el) {
      el.hidden = true;
      el.classList.remove('is-in');
    }

    function render() {
      if (!loggedIn()) {
        root.setAttribute('data-state', 'guest');
        bar.hidden = true;
        grid.hidden = true;
        hideState(empty);
        showState(guest);
        return;
      }
      hideState(guest);

      var list = savedIds().map(String);
      var shown = 0;

      items.forEach(function (li) {
        var on = list.indexOf(String(li.getAttribute('data-product-id'))) !== -1;
        li.hidden = !on;
        if (on) {
          /* Stagger index for the card's own fade — note 2. */
          li.style.setProperty('--i', shown);
          shown++;
          li.classList.add('is-in');
        } else {
          li.classList.remove('is-in');
          li.style.removeProperty('--i');
        }
      });

      root.setAttribute('data-state', shown ? 'items' : 'empty');
      grid.hidden = shown === 0;
      grid.setAttribute('data-count', shown);
      bar.hidden = shown === 0;
      if (shown) { hideState(empty); } else { showState(empty); }

      if (shown) {
        countEl.textContent = shown === 1 ? '1 item saved' : shown + ' items saved';
      }
    }

    render();

    /* The three signals assets/hov-wishlist.js:76-97 emits, plus a bfcache
       restore — a back-navigation must not show a stale grid. */
    document.addEventListener('hov:wishlist:changed', render);
    window.addEventListener('storage', function (e) {
      if (!e.key || e.key === storageKey()) render();
    });
    window.addEventListener('pageshow', function (e) { if (e.persisted) render(); });
    try {
      var bc = new BroadcastChannel('hov_wishlist_channel');
      bc.onmessage = render;
    } catch (e) { /* Safari < 15.4: the storage event still covers other tabs */ }
  }

  function boot() {
    var roots = document.querySelectorAll('[data-sh-wishlist]');
    for (var i = 0; i < roots.length; i++) init(roots[i]);
  }

  document.readyState === 'loading'
    ? document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', boot)
    : boot();

  document.addEventListener('shopify:section:load', boot);
})();
</script>

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "SH · Wishlist",
  "class": "index-section",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "header", "content": "Cards" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "atc_label", "label": "Add-to-cart button text", "default": "Add to cart",
      "info": "Set in uppercase by the stylesheet — type it in sentence case." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "soldout_label", "label": "Sold-out text", "default": "Sold out" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "When nothing is saved" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "empty_title", "label": "Heading", "default": "Your wishlist is empty" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "empty_text", "label": "Supporting line",
      "default": "Save items you love and find them here." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "empty_cta_label", "label": "Button text", "default": "Explore products" },
    { "type": "url", "id": "empty_cta_link", "label": "Button link",
      "info": "Leave empty to point at the first product in the catalogue." },

    { "type": "header", "content": "When the shopper is signed out" },
    { "type": "paragraph", "content": "Saving requires an account, so a signed-out shopper can never have a wishlist. They see this instead of the empty state." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "guest_title", "label": "Heading", "default": "Sign in to see your saved items" },
    { "type": "textarea", "id": "guest_text", "label": "Supporting line",
      "default": "Your wishlist travels with your account, so your saved rituals are waiting whenever you return." },
    { "type": "text", "id": "guest_cta_label", "label": "Button text", "default": "Sign in" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "guest_register_label", "label": "Secondary link text", "default": "Create an account" },

    { "type": "header", "content": "Appearance" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "animate", "label": "Animate on scroll", "default": true,
      "info": "Applies to the empty and sign-in states. Saved cards always fade in as they are revealed." },
    { "type": "color", "id": "bg", "label": "Background", "default": "#f6ede1",
      "info": "Keep it light — the text colours are tuned for a light surface. It sits under the cream page header, so a half-step deeper reads as a seam rather than a repeat." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "pad_top", "label": "Top padding", "min": 0, "max": 140, "step": 4, "default": 72, "unit": "px" },
    { "type": "range", "id": "pad_bottom", "label": "Bottom padding", "min": 0, "max": 140, "step": 4, "default": 96, "unit": "px" }
  ],
  "presets": [ { "name": "SH · Wishlist" } ]
}
{% endschema %}
